"text": " Real Madrid fans standing up to applaud a Barcelona player in their own stadium. November 19th, 2005. The Cl\u00e1sico at the Bernabeu. Barcelona were already 1-0 up. Then Ronaldinho picked up the ball on the left, ran at Sergio Ramos, went past him and fired it in. 2-0. 18 minutes later, he did it again. Past Ramos and low under Eka Casillas. 3-0. And then something strange happened. Thousands of Madrid fans rose to their feet and clapped. Before him, the only Barcelona player said to get that honour was Diego Maradona in 1983. Nine days later, Ronaldinho won the Ballon d'Or. Would your fans ever clap for a rival? Tell me in the comments. you",
